WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.739
The children stood around Huey's well without speaking.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.182
They had agreed to make two wishes each.

3
00:00:06.183 --> 00:00:08.884
Only Panther had one wish left.

4
00:00:08.885 --> 00:00:11.751
"Are you going to stand there all day?"

5
00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:14.386
Huey said, sounding irritated.

6
00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:16.341
Cy nudged Panther.

7
00:00:16.342 --> 00:00:18.812
"It's your turn," he said.

8
00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:21.913
Panther nodded but didn't say anything.

9
00:00:21.914 --> 00:00:25.514
"Are you running out of wishes?" Huey asked.

10
00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:27.956
Panther still did not speak.

11
00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:30.617
Bobby let out a loud sigh.

12
00:00:30.618 --> 00:00:32.438
Jane tapped her foot.

13
00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:34.723
Cy kept turning his head.

14
00:00:34.724 --> 00:00:37.237
Clearly they were all annoyed.

15
00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:39.186
But no one said a word.

16
00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:44.301
"I wish everyone would say what they are thinking," Panther blurted out.

17
00:00:44.302 --> 00:00:47.779
Huey's fins started to open and close.

18
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.600
Panther put her hand over her mouth.

19
00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:55.007
"No, Huey. That wasn't a wish," she cried.

20
00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:57.085
"But you wished it,"

21
00:00:57.086 --> 00:01:00.746
Huey said, his fins turning purple and blue.

22
00:01:00.747 --> 00:01:04.866
"What I meant was . . ." Panther tried to explain.

23
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:06.801
But it was too late.

24
00:01:06.802 --> 00:01:08.936
Huey granted her wish.

25
00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:12.110
"Now go away," he said.

26
00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:14.460
Cy placed Huey in the bucket.

27
00:01:14.461 --> 00:01:17.270
As he lowered him down, Cy muttered,

28
00:01:17.271 --> 00:01:21.335
"I'm sick of doing this every time."

29
00:01:21.336 --> 00:01:23.977
His siblings stared at him.

30
00:01:23.978 --> 00:01:26.846
Cy slapped a hand over his mouth.

31
00:01:26.847 --> 00:01:30.629
"Why did I say that?" he said in a surprised voice.

32
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.200
"That's because you're mean," Jane cried out.

33
00:01:34.201 --> 00:01:37.088
She, too, then covered her mouth.

34
00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:40.964
The children suddenly felt uneasy with each other.

35
00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:44.495
"I think we should go home," Panther suggested.

36
00:01:44.496 --> 00:01:46.823
The children headed out of the woods.

37
00:01:46.824 --> 00:01:49.528
Panther walked ahead of the others.

38
00:01:49.529 --> 00:01:51.613
She had much to think about.

39
00:01:51.614 --> 00:01:56.561
Suddenly Cy called out from behind, "Will you slow down?"

40
00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:59.252
Panther spun her head around and shouted:

41
00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:01.063
"Why don't you walk faster?

42
00:02:01.064 --> 00:02:03.091
You're such a slowpoke!"

43
00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:08.225
"Slowpoke? Who are you calling slow?" yelled Cy.

44
00:02:08.226 --> 00:02:11.198
"You always think you're better than us!"

45
00:02:11.199 --> 00:02:15.044
"Well, I am!" Panther shouted back.

46
00:02:15.045 --> 00:02:18.449
"Shut up, both of you!" exploded Bobby.

47
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.205
Stunned, Panther and Cy stared at their younger brother.

48
00:02:23.206 --> 00:02:25.758
"Did you tell me to shut up?"

49
00:02:25.759 --> 00:02:28.616
Cy said in a low, angry voice.

50
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:33.492
"Yes! You're acting like two baboons!" Bobby shouted.

51
00:02:33.493 --> 00:02:38.373
"You're the one who looks like a monkey," Jane yelled at Bobby.

52
00:02:38.374 --> 00:02:43.356
Soon all four children were shouting and screaming at each other.

53
00:02:43.357 --> 00:02:49.558
"So this is how you really feel about me," wept Panther.

54
00:02:49.559 --> 00:02:54.723
"I thought you cared about me," cried Bobby.

55
00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:58.424
After a while, the children ran out of things to say.

56
00:02:58.425 --> 00:03:03.735
"This is the worst wish ever," sniffed Jane.

57
00:03:03.736 --> 00:03:08.324
Panther didn't say anything because in her heart she agreed.

58
00:03:08.325 --> 00:03:12.560
Without speaking to one another, they all continued to walk.

59
00:03:12.561 --> 00:03:16.927
As they got closer to town, the children heard shouting everywhere.

60
00:03:16.928 --> 00:03:21.503
"I don't like you!" shouted Mr. Keefer to a young woman.

61
00:03:21.504 --> 00:03:26.112
"Well, I never liked you either!" she shouted back.

62
00:03:26.113 --> 00:03:29.359
Then the children spotted Aunt Martha with Lamb.

63
00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.028
She was speaking with Farmer Jenkins' wife.

64
00:03:32.029 --> 00:03:36.269
"Your hairstyle is ugly!" Mrs. Jenkins said.

65
00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.918
"What?" Aunt Martha touched her hair.

66
00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:44.111
"Well, you dress like a fisherman!" she said.

67
00:03:44.112 --> 00:03:50.337
"Oh, really? It's better than dressing like an old lady!" Mrs. Jenkins shouted.

68
00:03:50.338 --> 00:03:53.673
The two women looked as if they were going to wrestle.

69
00:03:53.674 --> 00:03:55.555
Panther ran up to them.

70
00:03:55.556 --> 00:03:59.560
"You don't mean that," she said in a pleading voice.

71
00:03:59.561 --> 00:04:02.218
"You two are friends."

72
00:04:02.219 --> 00:04:06.456
"She's no friend of mine!" yelled Aunt Martha.

73
00:04:06.457 --> 00:04:11.217
"She's certainly not my friend!" Mrs. Jenkins shot back.

74
00:04:11.218 --> 00:04:13.934
Panther's eyes filled with tears.

75
00:04:13.935 --> 00:04:19.666
"Oh, what have I done?" she moaned.

